* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Vendored third-party libraries are stored byte for byte. Without this,
# `* text=auto eol=lf` above rewrites CRLF in leaflet.css and LICENSE, and a
# fresh clone no longer matches the SHA-512 digests recorded as proof of
# provenance in assets/leaflet/README.md.
assets/leaflet/** -text
assets/markercluster/** -text

# Neither of these belongs in a distributed copy of the plugin. `tests/` calls
# `shell_exec()`, which is something the human reviewers at WordPress.org stop
# on, and `docs/` is a quarter of a megabyte of prose about how the plugin was
# built rather than about how to use it.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING IT TO DO THAT. `export-ignore` is honoured by
# `git archive` and by nothing else. It is what keeps these out of a GitHub
# release tarball, and it has **no effect at all** on a WordPress.org build:
# the directory is served from SVN, and a zip built by copying a checkout, by
# `wp dist-archive`, or by the deploy action everybody uses reads `.distignore`
# — a file this repository does not have yet. Task 25 owns writing it, and
# these two lines are not a substitute for it.
docs/ export-ignore
tests/ export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
.gitignore export-ignore
